---
import Learn from '../../layouts/Learn.astro';
import MemoryFlow from '../../components/learn/MemoryFlow.astro';
import BarChart from '../../components/learn/BarChart.astro';
import { COMPANY, PRICES, TRIAL } from '../../data/site';

// Learn comparison page 5 (s94). Rules: see ai-memory-apps-compared.astro and
// data/pricing.ts. Facts read on memoryplugin.com on 2026-10-13: Core $89 a year,
// Pro $180 a year, 7-day trial, 14-day refund, no monthly amount shown in the
// page text; Core keeps chat history to the last 500 conversations, Pro adds a
// knowledge graph (early beta), summaries, insights, shared buckets; "21+ AI
// tools" incl. ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, Grok, Perplexity, Cursor, Claude Code,
// Codex; browser extension, a Custom GPT (works in ChatGPT's iOS and Android
// apps), an MCP server for Claude Desktop and Claude Code; "Encrypted in transit
// and at rest"; "never sold, and never used to train models"; storage location
// not stated. Same need as Zaaheen (an everyday user's memory across AI apps),
// so the price chart compares them, as the Pricing page does.
const CHECKED = '13 October 2026';
const OUTLINE = [
  { id: 'what', title: 'What MemoryPlugin is' },
  { id: 'differ', title: 'Where Zaaheen differs' },
  { id: 'price', title: 'What a year costs' },
  { id: 'better', title: 'Where MemoryPlugin is the better choice' },
  { id: 'limits', title: 'Where Zaaheen falls short' },
];
const MP = 'https://www.memoryplugin.com/';
---
<Learn
  path="/learn/memoryplugin-alternative/"
  lede={`MemoryPlugin gives more than 20 AI tools one memory, kept by its own service, from $89 a year. Zaaheen does a similar job for the AI apps on your computer, with your memories encrypted on that computer instead, for $${PRICES.yearly} a year. MemoryPlugin reaches further, including ChatGPT on the web and your phone; Zaaheen keeps your memories closer.`}
  outline={OUTLINE}
>
  <section id="what">
    <h2>What MemoryPlugin is</h2>
    <p>MemoryPlugin connects a long list of AI tools to one memory, "21+ AI tools" in its own words,
       among them ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, Grok, Perplexity, Cursor, Claude Code and Codex
       (<a href={MP}>MemoryPlugin's site</a>). It gets there several ways: a browser extension for
       AI websites, a custom GPT that also works in ChatGPT's phone apps, and an MCP server for
       Claude Desktop and Claude Code.</p>
    <p>Its service keeps your memories, and the site says they are "Encrypted in transit and at
       rest" and never sold or used to train models. It doesn't say where they are stored. Core
       costs $89 a year and keeps your last 500 conversations of chat history; Pro is $180 a year
       and adds features such as a knowledge graph and shared buckets. Both come with a 7-day
       trial.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="differ">
    <h2>Where Zaaheen differs</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Where your memories are kept.</strong> With Zaaheen they never leave your
          computer: they are encrypted there, and our servers handle only sign-in and your
          subscription.</li>
      <li><strong>Price.</strong> ${PRICES.yearly} a year or ${PRICES.monthly} a month, after
          {TRIAL.days} days free with no card.</li>
      <li><strong>How apps connect.</strong> Zaaheen connects through MCP to the apps on your
          computer: Claude Desktop, Claude Code, Cursor, the ChatGPT app, Codex and others. There is
          no browser extension.</li>
    </ul>

    <MemoryFlow
      id="flow-memoryplugin"
      from="Claude"
      to="ChatGPT"
      fact="Prefers meetings after 2pm"
      others={['Cursor', 'Codex']}
      caption="A preference you mention to Claude is saved once to the memory on your computer, and the ChatGPT app reads it from there."
    />
  </section>

  <section id="price">
    <h2>What a year costs</h2>
    <BarChart
      id="chart-memoryplugin-year"
      title="One year for one person, in US dollars"
      measure="US dollars a year"
      bars={[
        { label: 'Zaaheen', value: PRICES.yearly, note: 'yearly plan' },
        { label: 'MemoryPlugin Core', value: 89, note: 'yearly plan' },
        { label: 'MemoryPlugin Pro', value: 180, note: 'yearly plan' },
      ]}
      source={{ text: `MemoryPlugin's own website and ours, prices as of ${CHECKED} and may change. MemoryPlugin shows these as reduced prices next to higher ones struck through.` }}
    />
    <table class="learn-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th scope="col"></th><th scope="col">MemoryPlugin</th><th scope="col">Zaaheen</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row">Where memories are kept</th><td>Its service, "Encrypted in transit and at rest"</td><td>Your computer, encrypted</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">AI tools</th><td>"21+", including AI websites and ChatGPT on phones</td><td>Apps on your computer that support MCP</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Trial</th><td>7 days</td><td>{TRIAL.days} days, no card</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Where it runs</th><td>Wherever its browser extensions, custom GPT or MCP server work</td><td>Windows, and Macs with Apple chips</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="learn-note">As of {CHECKED}, from MemoryPlugin's own website, and may change. Check
       <a href={MP}>their site</a> for the latest prices.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="better">
    <h2>Where MemoryPlugin is the better choice</h2>
    <p>If you use AI mostly in a web browser, on your phone, or in tools like Gemini and Perplexity,
       MemoryPlugin reaches places Zaaheen can't. Its Pro plan also lets you share memory with a
       team.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="limits">
    <h2>Where Zaaheen falls short</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No browser extension, so ChatGPT and Claude in a web browser can't use it.</li>
      <li>No phone version, and on computers only Windows and Macs with Apple chips.</li>
      <li>Your memory lives on one computer; there is no sync between computers yet.</li>
      <li>After the {TRIAL.days}-day trial there is no free plan.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="learn-note">MemoryPlugin is a name of its owner. We have no link with MemoryPlugin.
       Facts checked on {CHECKED}; if anything here is wrong or out of date, tell us at
       <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.email}`}>{COMPANY.email}</a> and we'll correct it.</p>
  </section>
</Learn>
